<title>POLAND: Polish bank sector climate index falls in May.</title>
<headline>Polish bank sector climate index falls in May.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's banking climate index fell two points to 47.3 points in May after holding flat in April, a poll released on Tuesday by the private Pentor institute showed.</p>
<p>The monthly survey showed the index called &quot;Pengab&quot; dipped slightly due to lower bank evaluations of zloty deposits.</p>
<p>The index, based on a scale of minus 100 to plus 100, polled 205 bank managers and is commissioned monthly by the Polish Banking Association (ZBP).</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
